WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.080
You’ve finally done it!

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.340
After years of adding movies and shows to
your queues, you’ve officially run out of

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.240
things to watch on Netflix.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.799
You’ve also exhausted your entire backlog
of books and you’ve even run out of cereal

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:17.100
boxes to read, so you’re left roaming the
streets in search of entertainment.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.280
That’s when you see a worn-looking flier
stapled to a nearby telephone pole.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.880
It’s an ad for a local community theater
production of a play you’ve never heard

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:27.880
of.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.400
A play called “The Hanged King’s Tragedy.”

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.539
Normally, you wouldn’t think of yourself
as much of a theater person, but something

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:36.899
about the art on the poster grabs you.

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:39.550
There’s a strange figure on the poster.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.969
Its face shrouded, its body wrapped in a web
of chains.

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:48.379
Your curiosity gets the better of you and
you check the performance date.

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:53.710
To your pleasant surprise, opening night is
a week from now, and you don’t have anything

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:54.710
planned.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.750
You’ve made up your mind.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:01:00.320
You’re going to attend a live performance
of The Hanged King’s Tragedy.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.840
It’s going to be the first live play you’ve
ever seen.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.490
And little do you know, it may also be the
last.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:13.680
Because The Hanged King’s Tragedy isn’t
just any old play - it’s a powerful and

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.479
deadly memetic hazard that may be one of the
gateways to an even more dangerous being.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:27.560
It’s known to the SCP Foundation as SCP-701,
so take your seats, be sure to read your programs

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:34.420
thoroughly, and prepare for the dark and terrifying
tale of The Hanged King’s Tragedy, and the

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:40.110
wave of death and destruction it causes in
its theatrical wake.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.720
But how could you know any of this?

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.420
While you head home to make dinner, looking
forward to seeing the new play next week,

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.370
the local thespians are hard at work performing
dress rehearsals.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:55.670
The director, one Marcus Fitch, happened upon
a copy of the play while looking for Carolinian

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.820
theater that’s a little more family friendly
than some of Shakespeare’s classics.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:05.659
When he’d first discovered The Hanged King’s
Tragedy on a theatrical forum, it was described

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:10.860
as being similar to Shakespeare’s Hamlet
and Titus Andronicus - but the violence was

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.510
largely offstage and implied, with a lot of
the play’s nastier elements glossed over.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.270
Perfect for audiences of all ages!

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:23.510
Given the fact that performances of The Hanged
King’s Tragedy tend to be mass-casualty

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:29.340
events - for reasons you’ll soon see - The
Foundation does everything they can to control

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.670
the spread of the play’s script.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.660
All copies are kept in a triple-locked vault
in a secure Foundation archive, which currently

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:42.280
includes two copies of the original publication
that are dated to the year 1640, twenty-seven

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:49.530
copies of the 1965 trade paperback edition,
ten copies of a 1971 hardcover printing, twenty-one

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:55.130
floppy diskettes containing the play script,
and one S-VHS video cassette tape containing

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:58.900
a live taping of one particularly infamous
incident.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:04.980
However, this seemingly does little to prevent
new performances of The Hanged King’s Tragedy

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.030
from occurring.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:12.190
The text of the play continually pops up online,
often under different or misspelled titles,

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:15.470
preventing Foundation web crawlers from keeping
track of them all.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:20.480
Nevertheless, the Foundation does everything
in its power to detect and stop performances

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.640
before they can go ahead.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.810
The danger of putting on or even viewing a
performance of The Hanged King’s Tragedy

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:32.690
cannot be overstated - it’s believed that,
in the almost 300 years since its original

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:39.090
publication, it’s claimed 10,000 lives through
performances at the very least.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.760
And if you’re in attendance, dying quickly
is one of the better outcomes.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.480
The origins of this memetic virus are just
as mysterious as the power that seems to drive

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.850
its effects.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:55.510
The play never has a declared author, and
the publisher - one William Cooke - disappeared

00:03:55.510 --> 00:04:00.170
from all historical records after the play’s
publication.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:04.260
Performances have been varied over the 300
years the play has been active - it’s been

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:09.860
spotted everywhere from British University
drama troupes to American high school plays.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:15.130
In what could have been an even more disastrous
tragedy, a television adaptation of the play

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:20.910
was almost broadcast by the BBC, before the
Foundation stepped in and put a stop to it.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:26.040
While its containment classification is currently
Euclid, scientists who have studied the play

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:31.150
have campaigned strongly to upgrade The Hanged
King’s Tragedy to Keter-Class - on account

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:37.260
of its unpredictability and tendency to manifest
across the globe with incidences appearing

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.000
decades apart.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.730
While members of the O5 Council are skeptical,
some researchers even believe that if given

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:49.460
a wide enough exposure, The Hanged King’s
Tragedy could cause a dreaded XK-Class End

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.260
of the World Scenario.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.190
It’s that dangerous.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:58.320
At this point you’re probably wondering
“what exactly is The Hanged King’s Tragedy?

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.790
What’s the play even about?”

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:06.150
As the name suggests, the play is a tragedy,
and takes place over five acts during the

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:11.410
Carolinian era, portraying the drama of the
royal court much like a number of plays from

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.450
that time did.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:18.180
It takes place in the city of Serko, the capital
of the mysterious, fictional kingdom of Trinculo.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.740
The focal point of the play is the conflict
between Gonzalo, the illegitimate king of

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.760
Trinculo, and Antonio, the true heir to the
throne.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.930
Before the start of the play, the previous
king of Trinculo, King Sforza, had been betrayed

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.700
and murdered by Gonzalo.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:39.560
Gonzalo led Sforza into the woods, where he
and his men subdued the king, and hanged him

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.430
from a nearby tree like a common criminal.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.120
Hence, The Hanged King’s Tragedy.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.350
However, Gonzalo is trying to keep his part
in the king’s murder a secret to keep the

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.130
throne for himself.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:55.710
But his guilt-stricken wife, Isabella, threatens
to spill the secret of Sforza’s murder.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:06:01.120
While Antonio tries to uncover the truth of
what happened in the woods, Gonzalo - in true

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:06.240
Shakespearean villain style - plots further
murders of his co-conspirators and loose ends

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:08.800
to keep his dark secret safe.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:14.300
This is where the play gets a little gruesome:
One enemy, Gonzalo has killed and cooked into

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.380
a stew.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:20.110
He then intends to use this stew to murder
his entire court with the help of an effective

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:25.000
and undetectable poison he was given by the
mysterious Ambassador of Alagadda.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.160
Though you’ll be pleased to know that this
tragedy has somewhat of a happy ending.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:35.590
In the end, Gonzalo is exposed and Antonio
claims his rightful place as King of Trinculo.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:42.130
Unlike his predecessor, Antonio decides to
show mercy, and Gonzalo is exiled to a monastery

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:46.320
for life rather than being executed for his
murderous ways.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:51.470
The heroes are rewarded, the villains are
punished, and all the deserving parties live

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.700
happily ever after.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.230
At face value, nothing seems off about the
play.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.340
If you’re familiar with other works of the
era, you might even find yourself getting

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:02.010
bored while reading it.

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:08.700
How can something this… normal, be the cursed
play that claimed so many thousands of lives?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:13.630
But the play’s unassuming nature only serves
to make it more dangerous.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:18.050
It doesn’t appear that the memetic hazard
is caused by simply reading the play.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:22.860
Like all good theater, it only truly comes
to life onstage.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:27.330
And your local production of The Hanged King’s
Tragedy is no exception.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:31.770
As your community’s amateur actors study
and rehearse the play, making sure to commit

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:37.139
every scene, every line, every single word
to memory - they don’t notice the little

00:07:37.139 --> 00:07:42.180
things that, to an outsider, might seem a
little...off.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:46.490
Occasionally, during group dress rehearsals,
actors will veer from the script.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:50.300
And we’re not talking about flubbed lines
or simple improvisation.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:54.980
No, actors will at times seem like they’re
reading from a completely different script,

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:58.120
and their fellow performers will respond in
kind.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:03.740
The play lulls you into a false sense of security
- stagehands, crew members, even the director,

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:08.840
all believe they’re performing the play
exactly as it was originally written.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.710
Ok so that’s not so bad.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.639
A play that changes itself.

00:08:12.639 --> 00:08:15.930
But things are going to get worse from this
point.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.620
Much, much worse.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:22.250
But hey, why let a deadly anomaly ruin your
evening plans?

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:25.080
You’ve been looking forward to seeing this
play all week.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:28.580
And you couldn’t seem to get that figure
from the poster out of your mind: All-black,

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:29.580
face shrouded, wrapped in chains.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:35.510
You have no idea that this entity is wanted
by the SCP Foundation, and that its designation

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:39.400
is SCP-701-1.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:45.990
All you want is an unforgettable theater experience
- and you’ll certainly get one.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:49.840
It’s a packed house, not an empty seat in
sight.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.740
The house lights dim and the curtain opens.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:58.220
Act 1 is quite normal, with all the back-stabbing
and royal court intrigue you’d expect.You

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.450
actually feel yourself getting a little bored.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.630
A big yawn escapes your mouth.

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:07.850
You’re thinking that maybe this was a big
mistake and you might sneak out between acts,

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.360
when just then, you see it.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:16.270
In the final scene of Act 1 you see the shrouded
figure, lingering in the background against

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:17.520
the curtains.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:23.730
He seems so still he’s almost like a shadow,
but as each act seems to run into the next,

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.910
he becomes more prominent.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:30.700
The rest of the cast never acknowledges him,
as they deliver dramatic monologues, but he’s

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.310
always there.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:39.110
Finally, the play reached Act 5 - the grand
banquet scene where it all comes to head.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:43.640
Gonzalo is preparing to poison his dinner
guests with his cannibal stew, while Antonio

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:47.800
and his allies plot to reveal his terrible
crimes and dethrone him.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:52.110
You find yourself so gripped by the drama
of it all, you almost didn’t notice that

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:58.030
the shrouded figure of SCP-701-1 was standing
right among the actors now.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:02.550
While, unbeknownst to you, the actors have
been deviating from the scripted story this

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:07.830
whole time, things are about to really take
a turn for the horrific.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:14.020
SCP-701-1, who is now known to the other performers
as “The Hanged King”, produces a blade

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:18.210
from thin air and passes it to the actor playing
Gonzalo’s wife.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:23.380
The actors onstage suddenly become entranced
- they attack and restrain Gonzalo, and a

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:26.380
noose drops down from somewhere above the
stage.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:31.320
The actors proceed to ritualistically hang
Gonzalo, before the actor playing his wife

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:36.610
stabs him to death, all while chanting “Blood
for the Hanged King!”

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.230
You should be horrified, but you’re not.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:44.570
You don’t even feel like yourself anymore,
and you’re loving everything that’s happening.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:48.450
Onstage, a series of other nooses fall from
above.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:53.460
Each actor grabs their own noose, and the
cast repeats “Blood for the Hanged King!”

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:57.560
before sacrificing their lives to the shroud-wearing
monster.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.589
If the carnage stopped there, it would be
bad enough, but this play doesn’t just drive

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:08.140
its players to acts of violent insanity - it
pulls the audience in, too.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.970
Before you know it, you’re pulled into a
vicious brawl with your fellow theater-goers.

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:15.270
There’s biting, clawing, punching.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.980
People hitting each other with chairs like
it’s a wrestling cage match.

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:23.830
It’s such a frenzy of random, senseless
violence that the building can’t contain

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:24.830
it anymore.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:29.490
You and anyone else who isn’t dead already
spill out onto the streets, and start attacking

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:31.690
everyone you can get your hands on.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:37.240
It’s transformed from a pleasant night out
at the theater into a full-blown riot.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:41.690
Even the police, sent in to control the situation,
are overwhelmed.

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:46.480
It isn’t until the SCP Foundation sends
a number of Mobile Task Forces trained in

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:50.610
advanced crowd control that the situation
finally begins to de-escalate.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.640
But you don’t care.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:58.459
Even when large men in Foundation tactical
gear are holding your arms, you still try

00:11:58.459 --> 00:12:00.300
to bite and kick.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:05.040
The effects of the play normally wear off
after around twenty four hours, but until

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:10.750
then the infected, including you, are just
rage-fueled monsters.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:14.490
In the end, it takes four adult men to properly
restrain you.

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:19.600
You’ll feel the bruises from their night
sticks tomorrow, but now, all you feel is

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:25.029
hate, and violence, and single-minded devotion
to something out there that you couldn’t

00:12:25.029 --> 00:12:26.300
possibly comprehend.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:32.830
And the whole time you’re screaming one
thing, over and over again “Blood for the

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:33.830
Hanged King!

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.500
Blood for the Hanged King!”

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:41.990
Now go watch “SCP - 610 - Zombie Plague
- The Flesh That Hates” and “SCP - 3999

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:47.790
- I Am At The Center Of Everything That Happens
To Me” for more horrific stories from the

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:49.370
files of the Foundation!

